-- title:
--   The source-band setup budget is bounded by the encoder ledger
-- statement:
--   Let $N,n,p,U,D\in\mathbb N$ with $N\le n$. Use the construction's band size $g_n$ and encoded-key modulus $m_n$, determined by its local half-width and block count. Here $p$ is the arithmetic modulus parameter, $U$ the input-magnitude parameter, and $D$ the shift-magnitude parameter. Let $E_n$ be the principal encoder count. The defined source-band setup budget satisfies
--
--   $$T_{\mathrm{setup}}(N,g_n,p,m_n,U,D)\le\bigl(1016(\log_2^{\mathrm{nat}}(U+1)+\log_2^{\mathrm{nat}}(p+D+1)+1)+1946\bigr)E_n+560.$$
--
--   This charges the original-array scan and complete packed band catalog to the encoder stage, retaining the explicit remainder-budget dependence.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SourceBandCosts.lean#L126-L140

